When Should You Use This Letter?
Use this letter if:
• You suspect fraudulent tax returns were filed using your personal information
• You are a victim of tax-related identity theft
• You need the IRS to investigate and correct records associated with your SSN or tax ID

Sample and What the Draft Includes
The draft typically includes:
• Identification of the victim (name, SSN, DOB)
• A brief description of the suspected fraudulent filing
• Reference to prior reports (police, FTC) if available
• A request for investigation, correction, and confirmation

Who Should Use This Letter?
• Victims of tax-related identity theft
• Individuals who received tax notices for returns they did not file
